=== aarch64-specific results ===
  * --enable-avx2 is REFUSED with "configure: error: --enable-avx2 is
    x86_64-only (this host is aarch64)" rather than silently accepted and
    ignored.  This is the intended behaviour of moving AC_ARG_ENABLE out of
    the amd64-only block: an option that cannot apply must fail loudly.
    (The first aarch64 run counted this as a FAIL because the harness, not
    the build, assumed x86_64; the harness was corrected, not the build.)
  * default build is AVX2-free and HAVE_AVX2 undefined, as on x86_64.
  * the hash-partition regression passes.
  * --enable-rseq, --disable-rseq, --enable-numa, --disable-numa,
    --enable-introspect all build; make dist -> tarball builds, passes
    make check, builds prop_palloc, and passes install-check.

=== the two KNOWN-PREEXISTING entries ===
test/debugger/test_inspect_e2e.sh's cached_skipped == 2 assertion failed here
in BOTH the default and the --disable-rseq configuration.  On x86_64 the
default build failed it intermittently (2/12) and --disable-rseq
deterministically (12/12); on this aarch64 host it failed in the default
build too on this run.  Same pre-existing invalid assertion (proven
independent of this workstream by a pre-Phase-4 rebuild on x86_64; see
2026-09-21-make-check-flaky-inspect-e2e.log).  Not retried, and counted
separately from PASS and FAIL.

Not established by this run: whether the aarch64 default-build failure rate
is higher than x86_64's 2/12 or whether this run was unlucky -- the per-run
rate was not measured on aarch64.

=== not covered ===
  * high-core-count aarch64 (arm-hi) -- this is an 8 vCPU box.
  * sanitizer/PGO builds; anything outside make check's 8 entries.
